                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5c40e4a-c227-37f0-888c-931c525a3d4b",
                        "entry_id": "6377d671-db77-3c64-9fab-d7e839902e11",
                        "glosses": [
                            "kierowanie popędu seksualnego do osobników tej samej płci"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b6ca270b-aa9e-4d57-97a0-c7770906c805",
                        "source_entry_id": "6377d671-db77-3c64-9fab-d7e839902e11",
                        "source_sense_id": "a5c40e4a-c227-37f0-888c-931c525a3d4b",
                        "target_lang_word": "homosexuality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "homosexuality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ccc561bd-7bb7-3b66-9f6b-ff3725d2d8ed",
                                        "entry_id": "5ea4aeb4-604c-3397-b0c5-70c84ea40677",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being sexually attracted primarily or exclusively to persons of the same sex, sometimes (potentially offensive) restricted to same-sex attraction between males."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54285195-de19-44f2-bfe4-b05d94f854da",
                                                "sense_id": "ccc561bd-7bb7-3b66-9f6b-ff3725d2d8ed",
                                                "text": "Great diminution or complete absence of sexual feeling for the opposite sex, with substitution of sexual feeling and instinct for the same sex. (Homo-sexuality, or contrary sexual instinct)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35e9cfbf-ad30-44aa-94c1-63cbd58ea6ef",
                                                "sense_id": "ccc561bd-7bb7-3b66-9f6b-ff3725d2d8ed",
                                                "text": "Some of the experts have gone into the question of homosexuality with great care, and advanced sundry learned and scientific theories in regard to that abnormal condition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "248a7bf6-c217-434a-8524-1d3bc9032f8a",
                                                "sense_id": "ccc561bd-7bb7-3b66-9f6b-ff3725d2d8ed",
                                                "text": "Of the dozen or so surviving articles, squibs, and letters to the editor, the most remarkable appeared in the Whip and Satirist’s February 12, 1842, issue, and disclosed the existence of a cabal of gay men in New York's otherwise wholesome nightscape of brothels and riots. Moreover it identified the spider who minced so delicately along the wide-flung strands of the sodomitical web. \"There is not one so degraded as this Captain Collins, the King of the Sodomites.\" He was a foreigner, an Englishman, in the long tradition of blaming homosexuality on the influence of aliens. Among the syndicate of perverts, the writer announced, \"we find no Americans as yet—they are all Englishmen or French\" (the English called homosexuality the French vice and the French the English vice; for the Whip it was the French and English vice)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43a7d574-f441-49f3-82df-7bf8d8761de9",
                                                "sense_id": "ccc561bd-7bb7-3b66-9f6b-ff3725d2d8ed",
                                                "text": "The state hierarchizes sexuality by defining homosexuality as an influence that corrupts minors. Such a discourse produces a notion of the correct sexual behavior that transcends into the political realm, reinforcing the heteronationalistic nature of the nation-building."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54dc6393-8545-374c-b6a7-e8864854104d",
                                        "entry_id": "5ea4aeb4-604c-3397-b0c5-70c84ea40677",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexual activity with a person of the same sex, sometimes (potentially offensive) restricted to same-sex sex between males."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9396766b-7c81-4dd8-be16-7a650d616a8e",
                                                "sense_id": "54dc6393-8545-374c-b6a7-e8864854104d",
                                                "text": "Bourneville believes that 75 per cent. of the inmates of the Parisian venereal hospitals have practised homosexuality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f73c37f9-3ef3-47d8-a05c-c0668b056a94",
                                                "sense_id": "54dc6393-8545-374c-b6a7-e8864854104d",
                                                "text": "A Prussian proposal for a harsh penal code made male homosexuality an even more serious crime."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f285c8e4-7dec-4a79-8fd7-d5dab57ba33b",
                                                "sense_id": "54dc6393-8545-374c-b6a7-e8864854104d",
                                                "text": "Third, it is possible to have gay sex with a crew member on your team. This isn’t possible with every crew member—only some, according to their pre-programmed sexual orientation. It’s obvious why this is an issue for Christians. Scripture explicitly says homosexuality is a sin (Genesis 18:20-21; 19:4-5, 24-25; Leviticus 18:22; Romans 1:26-27; 1 Corinthians 6:9-11; 2 Peter 2:4-10). Denying what Scripture says on it is nothing short of joyful ignorance and intellectual dishonesty.\nSociety, conversely, says it’s not a sin, and as such has thrown it into pop culture without a care for whom they offend. Obviously, for the Christian, do not go this route. If you believe homosexuality is a sin (and you should, considering God’s Word is inerrant and infallible and you say you’re a Christian), do not choose a gay romantic route. You may think it’s harmless if you do, but what’s the point in making a confession coherent with Scripture but not living according to that confession? Quite frankly, it’s hypocritical and needs repentance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "abbcfd31-2c84-4181-ba47-37c793a4e25e",
                        "source_entry_id": "6377d671-db77-3c64-9fab-d7e839902e11",
                        "source_sense_id": "a5c40e4a-c227-37f0-888c-931c525a3d4b",
                        "target_lang_word": "homosexualité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "homosexualité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3342319-e0e8-3418-941b-dbe898ef7135",
                                        "entry_id": "21c0c752-4c53-3d0f-9c58-1b4babef46c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Orientation sexuelle, attirance sentimentale et sexuelle pour des personnes du même sexe ou genre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03acd260-3311-4bc7-87fa-d9c36b42b1c6",
                                                "sense_id": "c3342319-e0e8-3418-941b-dbe898ef7135",
                                                "text": "Il me semble utile de réitérer ce que j’ai déjà dit ici même, et ce que M. Max Dessoir fait ressortir si bien : la profonde différence entre l’homosexualité, c’est-à-dire l’inversion, et l’hétérosexualité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cba61030-dec9-4bd6-871e-03d5911eedeb",
                                                "sense_id": "c3342319-e0e8-3418-941b-dbe898ef7135",
                                                "text": "Lorsque l’homosexualité intégrera la normalité, il faudra alors instituer le régime isosexuel où tous les rôles sexuels seront abolis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "229788d8-e810-4789-8305-c47e55467703",
                                                "sense_id": "c3342319-e0e8-3418-941b-dbe898ef7135",
                                                "text": "L’année 1973 aura marqué l’homosexualité moderne comme étant celle de sa sortie de la Bible de la psychiatrie qu’est le DSM (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95ed1993-3fac-4c8c-b3ec-022b927be617",
                                                "sense_id": "c3342319-e0e8-3418-941b-dbe898ef7135",
                                                "text": "En 1990, l’Organisation mondiale de la santé supprime l’homosexualité de la liste des maladies mentales, mettant fin à plus d’un siècle d’homophobie médicale."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98f9e6ed-2b92-3f16-a024-7341f7e9f229",
                                        "entry_id": "21c0c752-4c53-3d0f-9c58-1b4babef46c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pratique de relations sexuelles et affectives avec des personnes du même sexe ou genre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5810d9a-3ebc-4cc9-8777-d0f242c5d809",
                                                "sense_id": "98f9e6ed-2b92-3f16-a024-7341f7e9f229",
                                                "text": "Quant à la bestialité, elle heurte profondément les pratiques normales. Sa quête occupe davantage les juges au nord du royaume que l’homosexualité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "202f00d7-8480-408a-9453-b362f44b89b4",
                                                "sense_id": "98f9e6ed-2b92-3f16-a024-7341f7e9f229",
                                                "text": "Où l’on découvre que les hommes préhistoriques ne jouaient pas uniquement à « Moi Tarzan, toi Jane ». Leurs pratiques sexuelles étant nettement plus variées. Homosexualité, zoophilie, masturbation…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3de0c0e-adac-477b-97bb-429224b8248f",
                                                "sense_id": "98f9e6ed-2b92-3f16-a024-7341f7e9f229",
                                                "text": "Osons le dire : au sein de minorités sexuelles, les femmes prennent le pouvoir. Elles le font plutôt par la bisexualité que par l’homosexualité. Le drapeau arc-en-ciel ne doit pas nous cacher que le bloc historique LGBT est passé en matridominance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6715faa-04e8-4901-affc-8f74f89a4ef4",
                        "source_entry_id": "6377d671-db77-3c64-9fab-d7e839902e11",
